[21.056146, "o", "R1_ARM=L R1_ENTRY=implementor R1_ROUTES=coordinator=local,implementor=local,verifier=local,plan=local,implement=local,critique=local,smol=local M2_LOCAL_REPLAY=false\r\n"]
[264.118599, "o", "Done. `/app/solution.sparql` is written and verified.\r\n\r\n## The query\r\n\r\n```sparql\r\nSELECT ?professorName (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?country; separator=\", \") AS ?countries)\r\nWHERE {\r\n  ?professor a uni:Person ; uni:hasName ?professorName ; uni:role ?role ; uni:worksIn ?dept .\r\n  ?dept uni:belongsTo ?university . ?university uni:locatedInCountry ?country .\r\n  FILTER ( STRSTARTS( ?role, \"Professor\" ) )                 # 1 full professor\r\n  FILTER EXISTS { ... ?euCountry IN (27 EU codes) }          # 2 EU department\r\n  { SELECT ?professor (COUNT(DISTINCT ?student) AS ?currentStudents)\r\n    WHERE { ?professor uni:worksIn ?busyDept . ?course uni:isTaughtIn ?busyDept .\r\n            ?student uni:isEnrolledIn ?course .\r\n            OPTIONAL { ?student uni:hasGraduationDate ?graduationDate }\r\n            FILTER ( !BOUND(?graduationDate) || ?graduationDate > \"2025-08-16\"^^xsd:date ) }\r\n    GROUP BY ?professor ?busyDept HAVING ( COUNT(DISTINCT ?student) > 10 ) }   # 3\r\n}\r\nGROUP BY ?professor ?professorName ORDER BY ?professorName\r\n```\r\n\r\nDesign points: `STRSTARTS(?role,\"Professor\")` admits full professors while excluding `\"Assistant Professor …\"`; the country for `?countries` is collected in the main pattern over *all* `worksIn` departments, so non-EU posts still appear; criterion 3 is a group subselect counting distinct students per department (a student enrolled in two courses in the same department counts once).\r\n\r\n## Result on the given graph\r\n\r\n| ?professorName | ?countries |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Aristotle Tympas | GR |\r\n| Orfeas Menis | GR, US |\r\n| Pepe Attanasio | GR, PT |\r\n\r\nExcluded, with reasons: Marie Dubois (Sorbonne has only 6 current students — 8 of the 14 enrolled in Math201 graduated before 2025-08-16), John Smith (MIT, no EU department), Athanasios Voulodimos and Stefan Mueller (assistant professors). Current-enrollment counts: ComputerScience_NTUA 12, HistoryAndPhilosophy_NKUA 12, Engineering_Berkeley 11, Biology_MIT 7, Mathematics_Sorbonne 6.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\nNo SPARQL engine was available and the sandbox has no network (`rdflib`/`pip` absent, `curl` blocked by policy), so I parsed the Turtle and evaluated the query clause-by-clause in Python, twice with independently written checkers. Both reproduced the 3 rows above. The checkers also assert against the file on disk: all 21 expected graph patterns present, the `IN` list is exactly the EU-27 (no `CH`, no `US`, no omissions), and the reference date `2025-08-16` is used. Throwaway scripts were deleted, leaving only `solution.sparql`.\r\n\r\nTwo data quirks worth knowing: `Student5` references an undefined `uni:Bio10` (it joins nothing, so it silently contributes no enrollment — it does not affect any count here), and the file uses CRLF line endings.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.8-flash-next tools=54 surface=b1d6c95da52f\r\n"]
